A||N||2||FieroSTETZ||Think i solved the overheating||||1||
Z||000000||FieroSTETZ||06-15-2000||11:22 PM||||hmm- as a few of you may know, i have been having overheating problems as of late and have gotten nowhere. today, i was out looking at my car (no matter how mad i get at it, i always come back) and i remembered one time with my old SE when i accidentally started the car without the filler cap in the back (it sprayed water EVERYWHERE!)- this gave me an idea. i took the cap off the black fiero, started it up, and curiously enough, there was only a tiny bit of turbulence in the water- no spraying. well, i stuck my fingers in the water and it seemed to be flowing a tiny bit. my question is- does my waterpump sound bad? shouldnt it launch water everywhere without the cap on?||||reg||1
Z||000001||WKDFIRO||06-16-2000||01:53 AM||||Personally I have always worried about running the motor without the Therm cap on to get air in the system, but it is possible and has happened many times that the pully is turning but the impeller does not(at least in V6s). In which case that would be your problem. The pumps in question have plastic impellors. The good pumps have, I believe, stamped steel impellors. If you have tried everything else thats where I would go.<P>Good luck. Let us know what happens!<P>PS Fieros are sometimes like good women, no matter how much they agravate you, you keep coming back for more!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ditz88GT||06-16-2000||01:21 PM||||This is the same thing I just went through and it was the water pump.  The pump I pulled out had a plastic impeller and it was shot.  As soon as I replaced it, the car runs really cool.  Good luck and I hope it's the same problem.||||reg||1
